            <ArticleTitle>Concurrent presentation of appendicitis and acute cholecystitis: diagnosis of rare occurrence.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2014-208916</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2014208916</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 67-year-old woman presented with a 2-day history of central abdominal pain migrating to the right upper and lower abdomen. On examination she was normothermic but tachycardic. Inflammatory markers were noted to be elevated with a white cell count of 18.5×10(9)/L and C reactive protein of 265 mg/L. A CT scan revealed dual pathology of appendicitis and acute cholecystitis, which was confirmed intraoperatively and histologically.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
